	(text "CONNECTOR INVENTORY, SETTLED IN COPPER -- the 28-vs-18 dispute from the criteria round.\n  RCA line inputs        J51-J54    4\n  RCA outputs AOUT1-12   J71-J82   12\n  RCA coax S/PDIF in     J40        1   (on 05_spdif)\n  ------------------------------------\n  TOTAL RCA-CLASS JACKS            17\n  plus: speaker-level 8-way terminal (J60), power 2-way (J90), remote 2-way (J91),\n        and one 2x8 test header (J95).\nTHE OPERATOR'S COUNT OF 17-18 WAS RIGHT AND MINE OF 28 WAS WRONG -- I had added the 12\noutputs to a subtotal that already contained them. A total is an assertion; a sum is\ncheckable. This table is the sum.\n\nSPEAKER LEVEL IS A TERMINAL BLOCK, NOT AN RCA. At 30 Vrms the source is an amplifier\noutput pair, delivered on harness wire, and it is differential -- so it gets a screw\nterminal and shares the SAME differential nets as the line jacks. The RCA sleeve is\nIN{n}_N, which is what lets a single-ended source drive a differential receiver: the\nsleeve is not ground here, it is the inverting input, and grounding it at the jack\nwould throw away the CMRR the INA1650 and its matched attenuator were bought for."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 469.90000000000003 39.37 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "2eecc66b-8af5-572c-8139-753446e1a472")
	)
	(text "REMOTE-OUT IS FAIL-SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION (S7.4), AND THAT IS WHY IT IS A HIGH-SIDE FET.\nQ91 is a P-FET from VBATT_PROT; Q90 pulls its gate down when REMOTE_OUT_EN is asserted.\n  ENERGISED = ASSERTED. De-energised = released.\nTHE WALK: rails sag -> Q90's base drive dies -> R(gate-to-source) pulls the gate to\nVBATT_PROT -> Q91 turns OFF -> REMOTE_OUT RELEASES. This happens BEFORE the MCU knows\nanything, which is the entire point: S7.3 step 1 says remote-out drops first so the\ndownstream amplifiers mute before our rails finish collapsing. A LOW-SIDE switch or a\nGPIO-driven latch would both hold their last state into the sag -- exactly wrong.\nD90 (15 V) clamps Vgs against the VBATT_PROT excursions the TVS lets through; the same\nreasoning as Q2's gate zener on 01_power, and for the same reason it is not optional.\n100R to ground bleeds the line so a floating amplifier input cannot self-assert.\n\nCHASSIS / SHIELD (S6.3): the RCA shield field is a SINGLE net (RCA_SHIELD) star-joined\nto chassis through ONE RC -- 10R + 100n in parallel with 1M. The 1M bleeds static, the\n100n gives RF a low-impedance path, the 10R stops it being a plain short. Drawn ONCE,\nhere, and referenced from 05_spdif -- a second RC elsewhere makes a loop, which is the\nfailure this arrangement exists to prevent. It is an EMC component, per S7.5.\n\nTEST HEADER: grounds INTERLEAVED between signals per S4's note -- every odd pin is a\nsignal, every even pin is ground. On a 0.1 inch header carrying 12.288 MHz TDM that is\nnot tidiness, it is the return path; without it the header is eight unshielded stubs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 469.90000000000003 190.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "288d9077-f596-5f64-a2e9-3d9a9fd4c0ca")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
